From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostics: name the regions, not just the buckets.

Thread creation fails at a dozen threads because flexible memory is gone
-- 3072K left, and the 256 KiB retry 0868 added is taken where the 1 MiB
one is refused. log_flexible_holders says where it went, and then cannot
say which allocator:

    flexible_holders available=3072K mapped=461024K unnamed=0K buckets=29
    flexible_holder rank=1 bytes=378880K count=24 prot=0x3 name=orbis

370 MiB of 461 MiB in one bucket. "orbis" is simply what the kernel calls
an ordinary anonymous mapping, so that bucket is every plain mmap in the
process summed together, and the name distinguishes nothing.

Twenty-four regions averaging 15 MiB each is a specific enough shape to
chase, but only with addresses: an address can be matched against what
this port maps where -- the frame boxes, the Wine heap's blocks, the
guest's own memory, RADV's -- and a bucket name cannot. So list the
largest individual regions with their addresses, alongside the buckets.

Only on the path that already logs, which is entered once below 64 MiB and
once below 4 MiB.
diff --git a/native/wine64_main.c b/native/wine64_main.c
index 12039c7..106add4 100644
--- a/native/wine64_main.c
+++ b/native/wine64_main.c
@@ -291,6 +291,48 @@ static void log_flexible_holders(size_t available)
     PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 flexible_holders available=%zuK mapped=%lluK unnamed=%lluK buckets=%u overflow=%u",
                available >> 10, (unsigned long long)(total >> 10), (unsigned long long)(unnamed >> 10), used,
                other);
+    /* ⚠ And the individual regions, because the bucket above cannot answer
+     * the question it raises. Everything plain mmap returns is named "orbis"
+     * by the kernel, so one bucket swallowed 370 MiB of 461 MiB in 24
+     * mappings and said nothing about which allocator made them. An address
+     * and a size can be matched against what the port maps where; a bucket
+     * name cannot. Largest first, and only on this already-rare path. */
+    {
+        enum { REGIONS = 12 };
+        struct { uintptr_t start; uint64_t bytes; int32_t protection; char name[33]; } top[REGIONS];
+        unsigned held = 0;
+
+        memset(top, 0, sizeof(top));
+        address = 0;
+        for (unsigned steps = 0; steps < 200000; steps++) {
+            uint64_t bytes;
+            unsigned slot;
+
+            memset(&info, 0, sizeof(info));
+            if (sceKernelVirtualQuery((const void *)address, 1, &info, sizeof(info)) ||
+                info.end <= address) break;
+            address = info.end;
+            if (!(info.flags & 1)) continue;
+            bytes = info.end - info.start;
+            if (held == REGIONS && bytes <= top[REGIONS - 1].bytes) continue;
+            slot = held < REGIONS ? held++ : REGIONS - 1;
+            top[slot].start = (uintptr_t)info.start;
+            top[slot].bytes = bytes;
+            top[slot].protection = info.protection;
+            info.name[sizeof(info.name) - 1] = 0;
+            memcpy(top[slot].name, info.name, sizeof(info.name));
+            while (slot && top[slot].bytes > top[slot - 1].bytes) {
+                __typeof__(top[0]) swap = top[slot];
+                top[slot] = top[slot - 1];
+                top[slot - 1] = swap;
+                slot--;
+            }
+        }
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < held; i++)
+            PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 flexible_region rank=%u at=%p bytes=%lluK prot=%#x name=%s",
+                       i + 1, (void *)top[i].start, (unsigned long long)(top[i].bytes >> 10),
+                       (unsigned)top[i].protection, top[i].name[0] ? top[i].name : "-");
+    }
     for (unsigned rank = 0; rank < TOP && rank < used; rank++) {
         unsigned best = rank;
         for (unsigned i = rank + 1; i < used; i++)
